# Arts and Crafts' edges: a level 75 Warrior, the quest accepted (a GM), Led Astray available. Mhasbaf: 510 and Led
# Astray's 808 (Progress events alike: the two cycle, 510 first); 510's finish: bit 1; 808's: Led
# Astray begun. At Stage 0 a trade of a bowl (a GM): nil (no Hadahda script: nothing). Bits 1-7 (a GM: Prog 254) with a
# full bag: Hadahda 517, finished: the bowl does not fit: Prog and Stage kept; Hadahda 517 again; freed: the bowl, Prog
# 0, Stage 1. A trade of the bowl and a second item: nil. The bowl alone with a full bag: 573, finished: the Imperial
# Bronze Piece does not fit: no completion (the bowl kept); freed: 573: completed.
lists AhtUrhganWhitegate/Hadahda/onTrigger AhtUrhganWhitegate/Hadahda/onTrade AhtUrhganWhitegate/Mhasbaf/onTrigger AhtUrhganWhitegate/onEventFinish/510 AhtUrhganWhitegate/onEventFinish/517 AhtUrhganWhitegate/onEventFinish/573
char zone=AhtUrhganWhitegate pos=54.701,-6,11.387 job=WAR lvl=75
quest AhtUrhgan.ArtsAndCrafts accepted
item BowlOfSutlac
item SheetOfParchment
login
trigger Mhasbaf                         # 510 first (Progress events alike with Led Astray's 808)
finish
trigger Mhasbaf                         # the other one: 808
finish
warp -112.029,-6,-66.114 AhtUrhganWhitegate   # beside Hadahda
trade Hadahda BowlOfSutlac x1           # Stage 0: nil
finish-if-event
charvar Quest[6][1]Prog 254             # a GM: bits 1-7
fill-inventory
trigger Hadahda                         # 517
finish                                  # full: the bowl does not fit: nothing more
trigger Hadahda                         # Prog kept: 517
finish-if-event
free-inventory
trigger Hadahda                         # 517
finish                                  # a second bowl; Prog 0; Stage 1
trade Hadahda BowlOfSutlac x1 SheetOfParchment x1   # not the bowl alone: nil
finish-if-event
fill-inventory
trade Hadahda BowlOfSutlac x1           # 573
finish                                  # full: complete false: nothing more (the bowl kept)
free-inventory
trade Hadahda BowlOfSutlac x1           # 573
finish                                  # completed; the bronze piece; one bowl taken
